# Copper Linux
# Copper live session. The rootfs is a read-only ISO with a tmpfs overlay,
# so only /tmp (and the overlay) are writable. Real disk persistence is a
# later phase. /tmp shares the overlay upper by default; this entry only
# matters if something runs `mount -a`, so keep its cap in step with the
# overlay's (an ingot payload download plus its unpacked tree need the room).
tmpfs        /tmp     tmpfs   defaults,size=50%   0 0